0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Matt Sands teaches the decimal check as a three-step drill built on paperwork most owners already hold. Step one: dust) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (off the lease offer letter, which states your net mineral acres; an undivided one-quarter interest in a 640-acre section is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (160 net mineral acres, leased in the example at $1,000 per acre and a 3/16 royalty [tJr4jiz31fw @ 00:13:18]. Step two:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (pull the plat and permit from the state oil and gas commission site, or the spacing and pooling orders, to get the drilling) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (spacing unit, here 1,280 acres across two sections. Step three: 160 divided by 1,280 times 18.75 percent equals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (0.0234375, the number that should appear on the order for every well in that unit [tJr4jiz31fw @ 00:15:50]. Co-host) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (Justin Williams lists the toolkit: commission websites for spacing data, county clerk and recorder offices for ownership,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (Mineral IQ or a well database, and Sands's free net revenue interest spreadsheet, with a landman or oil and gas attorney) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (when records are thin [tJr4jiz31fw @ 00:17:14]. Inherited interests with no offer letter force a full title search from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (patent forward. Royalty Clerk's script closes the loop: ask how the payer calculated the decimal and request the net) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (mineral acres and unit acres it used [DN-VIoSmyF0 @ 00:04:18].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (The base formula breaks in predictable places, and practitioners name each one. In Oklahoma, a Blanchard interest) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (splits the royalty into the 1/8 statutory minimum plus a Blanchard slice, so a 3/16 lease shows as 1/8 plus 1/16 that the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (owner must add together; owning several tracts in one pooled unit likewise produces separate line items per tract that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (sum to the real total [tJr4jiz31fw @ 00:22:12]. Texas allocation and production sharing wells pay on lateral length) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (through your tract; Steven Hatcher's shortcut is to take the unit decimal and multiply by the share of wellbore in your) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (unit, so 50 percent of the lateral halves it [Z_HlEDh8-rw @ 00:06:37]. Richard Winblad adds that for Oklahoma) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (horizontals you need the percentage of perforations within your section from the survey [iD4uCjptCXM @ 00:06:27].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (On precision, Sands notes orders run to the eighth decimal place, irregular lots such as 39.08 acres instead of 40 cause) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (small mismatches, and an error in that last digit costs one penny per million dollars of revenue, so chasing it can burn) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (hundreds or thousands of dollars to recover cents [tJr4jiz31fw @ 00:29:18]. Royalty Clerk draws the same line: an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (eighth-digit mistake does not matter, a fourth-digit mistake does.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (The dollar stakes justify the drill. Mineral View models a well grossing $100,000 a month: a correct 0.015625 decimal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (is worth $1,562.50 before taxes and deductions, while an order showing roughly half, 0.0078125, pays about $781.25, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (gap of $9,375 a year and $187,500 over a simplified 20-year illustration [KYu7M4t5LAk @ 00:02:08]. Royalty Clerk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (shows how small errors compound: on 10,000 barrels at $70, the right 0.0097656 decimal pays $683.59, but a decimal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (2.7 percent low pays $665, leaving the owner $18.59 short every month on oil alone [blbomhUd0sA @ 00:02:22].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (Payment timing is the other negotiable lever. Sands says Oklahoma owners can elect a $25 minimum threshold so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (small or declining wells keep producing regular checks instead of one annual payment once a $100 threshold is hit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm ([tJr4jiz31fw @ 00:03:59]. Richard Winblad goes further, saying Oklahoma owners with proceeds between $25 and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm ($100 can request monthly payment. Royalty Clerk lays out the Texas clock: first payment from a new well within 120) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (days after the end of the month of first sale, then oil within 60 days and gas within 90, late-pay interest at two points) Tj ET
