BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 621.77 Tm (The most expensive failures start at the desk, not the rig. The Landman Class instructor says the firm never guesses) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 606.55 Tm (because they have seen four hundred thousand dollar and half-a-million dollar mistakes, and one guess can lose the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 591.32 Tm (client and every job the firm holds with them [ibeQr-rDmZ4 @ 00:35:50]. The same instructor warns that decimals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 576.10 Tm (occasionally fail, so landmen must teach themselves fractions, which matters when a 2.5-acre tract can carry 30 owners) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 560.87 Tm (and Oklahoma pays to the sixth decimal place [ibeQr-rDmZ4 @ 00:34:47]. Sebastian Cosme shows the trap in one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 545.65 Tm (deed: if John Smith owns 1/6 of the northwest quarter and deeds an undivided one-half interest to Kevin Baker, Smith) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 530.42 Tm (is left with nothing and Baker takes the full 1/6, because you can only deed out what you have; deed one half of my) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 515.20 Tm (interest instead and each holds 1/12 [-fWjBQtg9r4 @ 00:01:35]. Hatcher, who began writing drilling and division order) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 499.97 Tm (title opinions at a law firm, spells out the downstream cost: without confirmed rights, drilling through a tract is trespass,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 484.75 Tm (and the operator still has to know exactly whom to pay [ifwy0MQE0b4 @ 00:01:36]. Miss the words of my interest and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 469.52 Tm (every royalty decimal below that deed is wrong.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 454.30 Tm (The second trap is mistaking a check for a title. Matt Sands puts it bluntly: you could be collecting checks for years) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 439.07 Tm (while still not holding marketable title, because operators pay at a materially lower bar built around whether anybody) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 423.85 Tm (will credibly sue them, while buyers apply the higher bar and pay a premium for marketable title [sB8BNPnN_Os @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 408.62 Tm (00:22:57]. A paid-but-defensible interest draws discounted offers, and one heir's gaps can stall a whole family's sale.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 393.40 Tm (The math can also turn against curative: a simple probate runs about $3,000 to $4,000, which can exceed the value of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 378.17 Tm (0.1 net-acre interest, and an affidavit accepted on a $25-a-year vertical well can be re-reviewed the moment horizontal) Tj ET
