0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (nimbler, a lot cheaper, and more welcome to neighbors [8M30VzyjEpk @ 00:18:18]. Bit selection follows the hole) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (section: roller cone tricone and hammer bits in the vertical air-drilled portion, then synthetic-diamond PDC bits that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (shave the shale in the lateral, with mud jetted through the nozzles to cool the bit and carry cuttings [8M30VzyjEpk @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (00:09:40]. The British Columbia Energy Regulator supplies the tubular math: 30-foot joints at roughly 495 pounds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (each, over 350 joints weighing nearly 87 tons for a 10,500-foot well, with the string pulled for bit and tool changes in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (process called tripping pipe [qSA8EoDzhKo @ 00:02:07]. Every trip is rig time, so the bit plan matters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (The mechanics that keep the lateral alive live in the annulus. Offshore Engineering Academy gives the driller's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (formula: hole diameter squared minus pipe diameter squared, divided by 1029.4, equals annular volume in barrels per) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (foot, so a 12 1/4 inch hole around 5 inch pipe runs about 0.12 barrels per foot [YPFuHij-FYk @ 00:03:00]. That) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (number is the first line of defense against a blowout: if returns do not match what was pumped, the crew is either losing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (fluid into the rock or taking a kick, and both are stop-everything emergencies [YPFuHij-FYk @ 00:03:48]. The same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (channel warns that bigger pipe in the same hole speeds annular velocity and cleans the hole, but extra friction pressure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (can fracture weak rock, so hole cleaning versus breaking the hole is a constant balancing act. Dennis Livingston, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (Baker Hughes automated drilling systems technical advisor, describes the team with Consol Energy hitting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (two-mile-a-day Marcellus wells drilled under Pittsburgh International Airport, where the hard part was building a high) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (dogleg curve into a long lateral at proper ROP, landing in target and staying there [40uE_5Fvn_A @ 00:01:09]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (stated lesson from that record run was three words repeated: plan, plan, plan, with operator, service company, office) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (and rig personnel aligned on goals and communication holding through execution [40uE_5Fvn_A @ 00:01:45].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (Once production casing is cemented, the rig leaves and the service crew takes over. The British Columbia Energy) Tj ET
