BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 637.77 Tm (The first trap is the paycheck itself. Troy W. Eckard warns that the first royalty check arrives about six months after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 622.55 Tm (production starts and bundles one to five months of volume. The next check covers a single month, so it can come in at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 607.32 Tm (a third or a sixth of the first. Eckard's instruction is not to be alarmed but grateful for revenue captured fast) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 592.10 Tm ([nn1juJ3_-WA @ 00:08:21]. Mr. Business hammers a second gap: real checks are always lower than the headline) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 576.87 Tm (math. Regional differentials pull a $70 WTI print down to a realized $66 to $68, and post-production costs, 'cost-free') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 561.65 Tm (lease language fights and severance taxes chew on the rest [hIerB5MQ52U @ 00:11:07]. On gas, the same channel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 546.42 Tm (says deductions hinge on exact lease wording such as 'free of costs,' 'market value at the well' or 'proceeds received,') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 531.20 Tm (plus state law [8gaFGCKNpnk @ 00:15:08]. Then the buyers circle. Matt Sands states flatly that buyers will offer less) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 515.97 Tm (than value, and pairs that with a data rule: 18 to 24 months of unrestricted production before trusting any curve, since) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 500.75 Tm (curtailment, waterfloods and CO2 projects sit outside the standard fit [VYytHJ0lMVw @ 00:34:47].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 485.52 Tm (Model risk shows up in the inputs before it shows up in the checks. Ryan Hassen found that one apparent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 470.30 Tm (wellbore-azimuth anomaly was just a wrong EPSG code, and warns that if a GOR map is garbage, no machine-learned) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.07 Tm (relationship can save the forecast. The 100,000-well dataset also carries selection bias, because it covers only shales) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 439.85 Tm (that worked [qdJuFyTh5yU @ 00:12:19]. Mergers & Inquisitions built a hyperbolic type curve in Excel from a 10) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 424.62 Tm (MMcfe/d IP, a 60% initial decline and a 5% terminal floor. It landed at a 113% IRR and $15 million NPV10, against) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 409.40 Tm (Silver Bow's published 124% and $6.3 million, a gap the instructor pins on curve shape [2tJpxiIqFSM @ 00:15:17].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 394.17 Tm (Worse, issuers like Range Resources disclose EUR and D&C cost but no equation. That forces a goal-seeked 4 to 5%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 378.95 Tm (decline over roughly 25 years against a reserve life near 20, which the instructor calls a very common issue) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 363.72 Tm ([2tJpxiIqFSM @ 00:18:02]. Francis Ramos II adds a diagnostic check before any exponential math. Rate versus) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 348.50 Tm (cumulative must plot linear, and semi-log rate versus time must run as a straight line, while a plain linear) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 333.27 Tm (rate-versus-time chart does not reveal whether decline is exponential [u3kTgNXLIGI @ 00:02:47].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 318.05 Tm (Every forecast ends at an economic wall. TopDogEngineer solves for it directly, setting oil revenue plus GOR-linked) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 302.82 Tm (gas revenue minus operating cost to zero. In their Excel case the economic rate lands at 140.3 bbl per month; below it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 287.60 Tm (the well is losing money, and drilling and completion cost is pushed out to the NPV step [4mzbNb16NQc @ 00:08:49].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.37 Tm (The Crude Files notes that about three in four US wells already produce under 15 bbl per day. Plugging and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 257.15 Tm (abandonment costs run from tens of thousands upward, and orphan wells often land on taxpayers and states) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 241.92 Tm ([R-AasPj-Y5E @ 00:13:06]. Price can drag the wall forward. The Crude Files sets a Dallas Fed breakeven near $65) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 226.70 Tm (against 2025 oil in the low-to-mid $60s. ComboCurve reports core Haynesville gas not even at break-even, with JP) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.47 Tm (Morgan's roughly $3.50 core breakeven against about $3 gas [k4f-XlIpXZU @ 00:05:53]. Permian Resources shows) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 196.25 Tm (the defensive play. With Waha falling to negative $9.52, it choked back about 20% of gas by curtailing high-GOR) Tj ET
